WEBVTT

01:55.971 --> 01:59.971
NORTHERN ENGLAND EARLDOM OF NORTHUMBRIA
VIKINGS' BASE

02:02.641 --> 02:04.311
It was a Saturday.

02:04.851 --> 02:07.891
Vikings bathe on Saturdays.

02:11.361 --> 02:15.901
The English knew about this custom.

02:25.201 --> 02:28.001
Enemy attack.

02:35.461 --> 02:36.591
Burn them all.

02:36.671 --> 02:38.301
Don't spare the women or children.

02:38.921 --> 02:41.591
Kill them all. Those are the king's orders.

02:57.901 --> 02:59.531
SWORD

03:01.361 --> 03:04.071
Hang in there. This is it.

03:05.121 --> 03:06.201
Yeah.

03:06.291 --> 03:08.411
I killed Snorre.

03:08.501 --> 03:09.711
Damn.

03:10.371 --> 03:12.331
All right. Spear troops, advance.

03:12.501 --> 03:14.251
Charge.

03:21.221 --> 03:24.511
The battlefield went that way.

03:25.431 --> 03:28.771
Why do I always get killed so fast?

03:29.221 --> 03:32.811
Dead men aren't supposed to talk, Thorfinn.

03:33.271 --> 03:37.071
You're always the first one to die, Faxi.

03:37.151 --> 03:38.441
Yeah.

03:39.111 --> 03:44.451
In Valhalla, in heaven,
you get to eat meat every day.

03:44.531 --> 03:48.661
You can't enter Valhalla
unless you're a strong warrior.

03:50.501 --> 03:52.161
I see.

03:54.711 --> 03:58.631
I wonder if my mother and my sister
will get into Valhalla.

04:04.011 --> 04:05.471
Did they kill you, Thorfinn?

04:05.551 --> 04:08.181
If you die in the snow, you'll catch a cold.

04:12.141 --> 04:13.691
You're leaving tomorrow?

04:13.771 --> 04:16.691
You're so lucky. Where are you going this time?

04:17.191 --> 04:19.481
To Norway. I'm not going there for fun.

04:20.151 --> 04:21.441
I'm going to trade goods.

04:21.941 --> 04:26.201
I take wool and fur, and trade it for wine.

04:26.281 --> 04:27.951
Then I'm going too.

04:28.371 --> 04:32.121
No. What do you mean, "then"?
Don't say it so casually.

04:32.201 --> 04:33.911
What? You're so stingy.

04:34.001 --> 04:36.421
I don't care if you end up hitting an ice floe.

04:39.341 --> 04:42.091
I want to get some wine before the end of the year.

04:42.721 --> 04:44.801
I'm going to celebrate the birth of Jesus Christ

04:44.881 --> 04:47.181
with the people of my home country
with some wine.

04:47.681 --> 04:50.061
My father likes mead.

04:50.141 --> 04:51.311
Ask him for some.

04:52.851 --> 04:55.271
It has to be wine.

04:55.941 --> 04:59.731
I thought there'd be some wine in this village, though.

05:03.861 --> 05:04.741
Thorfinn.

05:05.361 --> 05:08.451
Can you pass on a message to your father for me?

05:08.531 --> 05:09.451
What?

05:10.121 --> 05:11.701
A warship has come.

05:23.671 --> 05:25.841
How's this, master?

05:25.921 --> 05:27.841
The leak's been fixed this time.

05:27.931 --> 05:29.761
Try putting some water in it.

05:33.431 --> 05:35.231
This is difficult.

05:35.311 --> 05:37.521
You put too much strength into it, Thors.

05:37.601 --> 05:38.901
Father.

05:39.311 --> 05:40.731
Father.

05:41.981 --> 05:43.401
I'm over here, Thorfinn.

05:43.861 --> 05:45.031
Father.

05:45.441 --> 05:48.411
Another warship came. It's huge.

06:06.131 --> 06:09.091
They asked for Thors the Troll.
They've been waiting there ever since.

06:09.721 --> 06:12.551
Thors? Are they talking about Thors?

06:12.641 --> 06:13.681
Troll?

06:13.971 --> 06:16.731
They're no amateurs.

06:17.271 --> 06:20.061
They're not like Halfdan's thugs.

06:21.651 --> 06:23.071
Oh, Thors.

06:23.731 --> 06:25.821
Are they planning to invade this village?

06:30.281 --> 06:31.661
Jomsvikings.

06:32.121 --> 06:33.581
I'm right here.

06:44.801 --> 06:46.341
They're bowing to Thors.

06:47.381 --> 06:50.471
I never imagined you'd come this far looking for me.

06:51.721 --> 06:52.801
Floki.

06:54.931 --> 06:58.561
We haven't seen each other
since the Norway campaign, Thors.

07:00.691 --> 07:03.941
I never imagined you'd be hiding here,
at the end of the earth.

07:04.981 --> 07:07.111
Tell me your business, Floki.

07:08.031 --> 07:10.991
Well, then. First give us your permission to land.

07:12.951 --> 07:15.371
Who is Thors?

07:16.201 --> 07:19.331
I heard he used to work on the battlefield
when he was young.

07:19.871 --> 07:21.421
They'll hear you, Ari.

07:22.291 --> 07:25.381
He doesn't talk about himself much.

07:25.461 --> 07:27.671
Let me see.

07:28.051 --> 07:30.841
He said "Jomsvikings," right?

07:30.921 --> 07:32.051
Know anything about them?

07:32.131 --> 07:33.221
Not really...

07:34.261 --> 07:36.721
Father is angry.

07:37.971 --> 07:41.731
They made a surprise attack while they were bathing.

07:42.311 --> 07:47.651
Many Danes were killed
by English troops in Danelaw.

07:48.531 --> 07:50.111
Gunhilde,

07:50.491 --> 07:52.991
the sister of Sweyn,

07:53.071 --> 07:55.701
the King of Denmark, was one of the victims.

07:56.371 --> 07:58.201
Revenge for his sister.

07:59.241 --> 08:01.791
King Sweyn has a good excuse now.

08:02.411 --> 08:04.881
A big war is about to begin.

08:04.961 --> 08:07.091
It's time for us warriors to shine.

08:07.541 --> 08:08.801
-War?
-Quiet.

08:09.341 --> 08:12.471
The Jomsvikings will join the army of Denmark.

08:12.801 --> 08:16.721
Our invasion of England will begin
this coming spring.

08:17.801 --> 08:19.101
Do what you will.

08:19.561 --> 08:21.981
This is a small village
at the northern edge of the world.

08:22.231 --> 08:26.271
Whatever these big countries on the other side
of the North Sea decide, it's none of my business.

08:28.941 --> 08:30.941
That will not do.

08:31.441 --> 08:36.661
Our leader Sigvaldi ordered me
to gather the entire fleet at Jomsborg.

08:36.741 --> 08:38.121
No exceptions.

08:38.831 --> 08:40.081
Do you understand?

08:40.541 --> 08:44.411
Even if that man deserted the army.

08:47.081 --> 08:48.421
Deserted?

08:51.881 --> 08:54.051
Captain of the Jomsvikings.

08:54.131 --> 08:55.631
Thors the Troll.

08:56.131 --> 08:58.011
This is a war...

08:59.641 --> 09:02.021
in which you too will fight.

09:14.651 --> 09:16.031
Thors.

09:16.451 --> 09:20.331
Our leader is doing this out of his own goodwill.

09:21.411 --> 09:24.371
After going missing 15 years ago,

09:24.451 --> 09:27.171
you have a chance
to return to the battlefield with honor.

09:27.581 --> 09:31.921
Our leader is willing to overlook everything.

09:32.001 --> 09:36.971
That's how much our leader wants you.

09:38.261 --> 09:42.181
You didn't have to come on a warship
just to tell me that.

09:42.261 --> 09:44.101
The villagers are afraid.

09:46.481 --> 09:50.061
You've changed a lot, Thors.

09:50.731 --> 09:53.361
Or did this village change you?

09:54.651 --> 09:56.191
-Run away.
-Run away.

09:56.821 --> 09:58.111
He's scary.

10:00.031 --> 10:01.031
This is a nice village.

10:01.531 --> 10:03.081
I can tell from the children.

10:03.661 --> 10:07.291
They've lived a life free from war, until today.

10:14.091 --> 10:15.711
Hear that? There's going to be a war.

10:15.801 --> 10:17.671
-Wow.
-This is my first war.

10:18.341 --> 10:22.301
He came all the way across the ocean to invite Thors.

10:22.391 --> 10:25.061
Your father is amazing.

10:27.181 --> 10:30.441
But I wonder if he'd take us with him.

10:30.521 --> 10:32.441
You have no chance. You're weak.

10:32.521 --> 10:36.111
-What are you talking about?
-You're no good unless you're strong.

10:36.191 --> 10:38.901
Well, I got that covered.

10:39.201 --> 10:41.821
You've never killed anyone, right?

10:41.911 --> 10:45.161
It all depends on whether
you've had that experience or not.

10:45.241 --> 10:46.201
Sorry.

10:54.251 --> 10:55.381
I'm not just...

10:56.131 --> 10:58.091
a powerless messenger, you know.

10:58.761 --> 11:02.261
If you're saying you're not going to fight in the war,

11:02.591 --> 11:06.681
I can't carry out my master's orders,
and our leader's reputation would be damaged.

11:07.471 --> 11:11.141
I can't go back empty-handed in a situation like that.

11:15.321 --> 11:16.941
You understand, don't you?

11:25.081 --> 11:26.911
The Jomsvikings.

11:27.701 --> 11:30.871
They're an army with a base in Jomsborg,

11:30.961 --> 11:32.791
a port town in Wendland.

11:33.381 --> 11:34.961
I never imagined

11:35.041 --> 11:36.841
that Thors used to be a Jomsviking.

11:37.251 --> 11:38.591
Are they strong?

11:38.671 --> 11:39.801
They're strong.

11:39.881 --> 11:41.431
They're so strong

11:41.511 --> 11:45.511
that the King of Wendland was unable
to collect taxes from them.

11:46.261 --> 11:49.311
They take pride in being the strongest army
in the Northern Sea.

11:49.391 --> 11:52.061
Withdraw. All troops, return to the ship.

11:54.271 --> 11:55.811
Withdraw.

12:02.901 --> 12:05.781
What was that just now? That was weird.

12:05.871 --> 12:07.871
You've been saved, Ari.

12:12.251 --> 12:14.041
Listen, villagers.

12:14.501 --> 12:16.921
I'm Floki of the Jomsvikings.

12:17.791 --> 12:19.841
At the orders of my master,

12:19.921 --> 12:21.341
I have come to this land

12:21.421 --> 12:24.091
to ask the hero Thors Snorresson to join our forces.

12:24.761 --> 12:25.841
Hero?

12:26.261 --> 12:27.681
Our leader has requested

12:27.761 --> 12:33.021
that Thors be provided with one warship.

12:33.601 --> 12:35.151
If you have what it takes,

12:35.231 --> 12:38.691
join Thors and come with us to Jomsborg.

12:46.741 --> 12:48.331
Farewell, Thors.

12:48.411 --> 12:50.911
We shall meet on the battlefield.

12:57.251 --> 12:59.341
We're going to war.

13:03.131 --> 13:06.431
-How many decades has it been?
-What?

13:06.511 --> 13:08.181
I'm going to kill them all.

13:08.261 --> 13:10.971
It'll be an honor to die on the battlefield.

13:11.061 --> 13:14.141
Let's get started right away.
Let's prepare the ships tomorrow.

13:19.151 --> 13:21.941
I guess you couldn't say no, Thors.

13:23.111 --> 13:25.201
I dragged the village into this.

13:29.121 --> 13:30.331
A long time ago,

13:30.411 --> 13:33.291
I used to earn my living by killing people.

13:34.331 --> 13:35.541
But one day...

13:36.711 --> 13:39.381
One day, I suddenly hated it all.

13:40.381 --> 13:41.501
I didn't want to kill

13:42.051 --> 13:43.421
or be killed.

13:44.631 --> 13:46.131
That's why I ran away

13:46.881 --> 13:48.301
from the battlefield.

13:53.181 --> 13:57.021
I thought I succeeded in making it look like I died.

13:57.521 --> 13:59.191
You could do that again.

14:02.481 --> 14:05.861
If I run away, this village will be punished in my place.

14:06.741 --> 14:10.031
The Jomsvikings never forgive deserters.

14:17.041 --> 14:18.671
The time has come

14:19.251 --> 14:22.171
for me to take responsibility
for what I've done.

14:29.801 --> 14:31.721
All right. Ready?

14:31.801 --> 14:33.811
One, two...

14:33.891 --> 14:35.931
Heave, ho.

14:36.471 --> 14:37.681
Heave, ho.

14:37.771 --> 14:39.311
Pull.

14:39.391 --> 14:41.271
Heave, ho.

14:41.351 --> 14:44.321
What? I thought you were leaving today, Leif.

14:44.771 --> 14:46.691
Thors asked me.

14:46.781 --> 14:49.491
I decided to join the fleet with that warship.

14:49.571 --> 14:50.701
I see.

14:50.781 --> 14:52.821
That would be safer.

14:53.201 --> 14:56.331
We'll protect you in a pinch.

14:57.581 --> 14:58.911
Here we go.

14:59.661 --> 15:00.961
I'm counting on you.

15:01.041 --> 15:02.751
Pull. Pull.

15:02.831 --> 15:04.091
Heave, ho.

15:04.171 --> 15:05.881
Though,

15:05.961 --> 15:08.301
everyone really does love war.

15:13.431 --> 15:15.311
You're so mean.

15:17.561 --> 15:19.601
Darn you, Thorfinn.

15:19.681 --> 15:21.101
Surround him.

15:22.151 --> 15:23.561
Bastard.

15:24.231 --> 15:26.781
We did it. I killed Thorfinn.

15:27.531 --> 15:28.901
That hurt.

15:28.991 --> 15:31.951
What's wrong with you? Die, Thorfinn.
You got killed just now.

15:32.361 --> 15:33.621
Follow the rules.

15:33.701 --> 15:35.701
That's right.

15:37.411 --> 15:38.371
What's wrong with you?

15:38.451 --> 15:39.581
Are you okay?

15:40.081 --> 15:41.461
Wait, Thorfinn.

15:48.421 --> 15:50.091
All right. Lift.

15:50.511 --> 15:53.591
One, two, three.

15:54.931 --> 15:56.851
All right. One more time.

15:57.101 --> 15:58.521
Thors.

15:58.811 --> 16:00.851
Can you take a look at this?

16:03.941 --> 16:05.111
The pain.

16:05.561 --> 16:06.861
It's broken.

16:06.941 --> 16:09.031
Someone hit too hard.
It's supposed to be a game.

16:10.401 --> 16:12.451
Keep the splint on for one month.

16:12.861 --> 16:14.861
Sorry, Thors.

16:14.951 --> 16:16.451
Thorfinn did it.

16:16.951 --> 16:18.621
He pisses me off.

16:18.701 --> 16:19.951
He's too rough.

16:20.041 --> 16:21.911
I'm never playing with him again.

16:22.581 --> 16:24.671
Is that true? My son did this?

16:25.041 --> 16:26.381
Yes.

16:26.501 --> 16:28.801
I'm sorry.

16:28.881 --> 16:30.421
I'll talk to him about this.

16:31.671 --> 16:32.881
Don't take it so seriously.

16:32.971 --> 16:34.301
It's between the kids.

16:34.881 --> 16:36.971
He's only 6, right?

16:37.051 --> 16:39.891
If he can hurt kids
that are four or five years older than him,

16:39.971 --> 16:41.181
he must be pretty strong.

16:41.851 --> 16:44.021
He'll grow up to be a good fighter.

16:44.101 --> 16:47.151
He takes after you, Thors.

16:59.281 --> 17:01.371
You're giving me all of this, Dad?

17:02.331 --> 17:04.541
They're family treasures from my grandfather.

17:04.621 --> 17:06.461
Fight with all your might.

17:06.541 --> 17:07.541
Ari.

17:08.631 --> 17:10.131
You look good, Ari.

17:10.211 --> 17:11.801
Look at mine.

17:12.261 --> 17:15.301
It can cut off a horse's head in one stroke.

17:15.381 --> 17:16.841
Wow, it's huge.

17:16.931 --> 17:18.641
Spears are what's best for plundering.

17:18.721 --> 17:20.431
Really? Want to have a match?

17:25.021 --> 17:27.231
What's wrong with you?

17:27.311 --> 17:29.861
Don't throw everything on the floor.

17:29.941 --> 17:31.441
Hey. Are you listening to me?

17:31.941 --> 17:34.611
I'm going to throw it away
if you don't pick it up. Got it?

17:34.691 --> 17:36.701
Go ahead. I don't want it anymore.

17:39.071 --> 17:42.491
What are you doing,
searching through the storage room?

17:42.581 --> 17:44.161
Where are our weapons?

17:44.251 --> 17:45.791
What? Weapons?

17:46.331 --> 17:48.291
I need a weapon.

17:48.791 --> 17:49.791
If I had a weapon...

17:50.751 --> 17:51.961
Are you thinking...

17:52.301 --> 17:56.131
you're going to become a warrior
and sail on your father's ship?

17:56.761 --> 17:59.841
I'm telling you now,
don't waste your time trying.

17:59.931 --> 18:01.811
A little kid like you can't do it.

18:06.061 --> 18:07.231
Thorfinn.

18:52.731 --> 18:54.191
It's beautiful.

19:05.871 --> 19:08.251
What is it? What's wrong, Ylva?

19:11.501 --> 19:13.961
Do you want a sword, Thorfinn?

19:15.631 --> 19:17.591
A sword is a tool for killing people.

19:18.511 --> 19:21.891
Who were you planning to kill with this?

19:23.721 --> 19:25.811
The... The enemy.

19:27.021 --> 19:29.731
Who is your enemy?

19:32.191 --> 19:33.061
Like...

19:33.521 --> 19:35.231
Halfdan.

19:39.741 --> 19:41.651
Listen closely, Thorfinn.

19:48.701 --> 19:50.541
You don't have any enemies.

19:51.581 --> 19:54.461
No one has any enemies.

20:00.011 --> 20:03.431
There's no one who it's okay to hurt.

20:07.721 --> 20:10.221
You're wrong.

20:10.601 --> 20:13.731
Father, you're going off to war tomorrow.

20:14.231 --> 20:16.191
You're going to kill the enemy, right?

20:18.401 --> 20:19.731
I'm not a kid anymore.

20:20.281 --> 20:22.111
You're lying, Father.

20:22.401 --> 20:23.911
I can tell.

20:26.031 --> 20:27.161
Thorfinn.

20:27.781 --> 20:29.371
Thorfinn.

20:29.451 --> 20:32.121
-You let your guard down.
-That was dangerous.

20:32.211 --> 20:33.291
Hey.

20:33.371 --> 20:34.831
You made me bleed.

20:41.801 --> 20:42.841
Helga.

20:43.881 --> 20:44.971
Yes?

20:47.101 --> 20:49.761
Take care of him for me.

21:08.491 --> 21:10.661
The wind blows faintly from the west north-west.

21:10.741 --> 21:12.331
The waves are calm.

21:13.831 --> 21:16.171
Odin is in good spirits this morning.

21:17.211 --> 21:19.751
This is a good morning for your departure.

21:21.091 --> 21:21.921
Indeed.

21:27.721 --> 21:32.021
FAROE ISLANDS
STREYMOY

21:33.981 --> 21:35.521
You said it.

21:35.601 --> 21:39.111
If I throw left-handed and hit it,
the barrel is mine.

21:39.191 --> 21:41.021
-No way.
-You can talk after you hit it.

21:41.111 --> 21:42.111
I beg you, God...

21:42.611 --> 21:44.571
Here I go, Christian monk.

21:44.651 --> 21:46.611
If you dodge, I'll kill you.

21:50.491 --> 21:54.041
You bastard. You dodged.
You dodged just now. I'm going to kill you.

21:54.121 --> 21:55.501
Move. It's my turn.

21:59.131 --> 22:01.091
Oh, no. The priest...

22:02.251 --> 22:04.211
I told you not to dodge.

22:04.301 --> 22:06.511
You're just bad.

22:07.591 --> 22:10.301
Hey, Jomsvikings.

22:10.391 --> 22:12.261
Want to have a drink?

22:16.181 --> 22:18.101
They have good manners.

22:18.191 --> 22:19.311
Leave them alone.

22:19.401 --> 22:21.771
They said they don't like cheap alcohol.

22:22.191 --> 22:23.021
Hey.

22:25.231 --> 22:27.451
How many points do I get for his leg?

22:28.991 --> 22:33.531
Your men don't have any class, Askeladd.

22:34.991 --> 22:39.081
We just hate Christians, Floki.

22:40.121 --> 22:43.291
Enough about that. Let's get down to business.

22:44.671 --> 22:49.841
My men and I are bored of being kept here waiting
in the middle of nowhere.

22:50.891 --> 22:52.601
There are no major changes.

22:55.771 --> 22:57.931
You will be compensated with five pounds of gold.

22:58.311 --> 23:01.441
I will only pay you in exchange for his dead body.

23:02.481 --> 23:06.361
You can do whatever you want with their ship,
and their cargo.

23:09.281 --> 23:11.491
Kill Thors.
